# SPEC GOLDEN — hand-written from CSS 2.1 §10.4 plus css-ui `box-sizing`,
# never regenerated. Both divs are written identically apart from the keyword:
# width 160px, padding 8px, border 8px.
#
# In cells: width 160px = 20 · padding 8px = 1 cell wide, 1 line tall (8/16
# rounds up, it is not zero) · border 8px = 1 cell wide, 1 line tall.
# Horizontal edges = border 1 + padding 1 on each side = 4 cells.
#
# .bb  border-box: the 20 cells *include* the edges -> content 20 - 4 = 16
# .cb  content-box: the 20 cells are the content    -> content 20
#      exactly 4 cells wider, which is the padding+border it stopped counting
#
# Content origin is border + padding either way: x = 1 + 1 = 2.
# Vertically both are 1 line of text inside 1 line of padding inside 1 line of
# border, so each border box is 5 rows: .bb owns 0..5, .cb starts at 5 and its
# content sits at 5 + 1 + 1 = 7. Page is 10 rows.
<html>  x=0 y=0 w=60 h=10
  <body>  x=0 y=0 w=60 h=10
    <div.bb>  x=2 y=2 w=16 h=1
      anonymous  x=2 y=2 w=16 h=1
        line  x=2 y=2 w=16 h=1
          #text "bb"  x=2 y=2 w=2 h=1
    <div.cb>  x=2 y=7 w=20 h=1
      anonymous  x=2 y=7 w=20 h=1
        line  x=2 y=7 w=20 h=1
          #text "cb"  x=2 y=7 w=2 h=1
